@startuml
title Planned booking collaboration - no business behavior implemented
actor User
participant "REST adapter" as Route
participant "BookingService" as Service
participant "EventKindPolicy\nStrategy" as Policy
participant "PriceHandler chain\nChain of Responsibility" as Price
participant "BookingState\nState" as State
database PostgreSQL
participant "WorkerDispatcher" as Worker
participant "NotificationSubscriber\nObserver" as Observer
participant "MailTransport\nAdapter" as Mail
User -> Route : create booking + idempotency key
Route -> Service : validated DTO and authenticated actor
Service -> PostgreSQL : begin; authorize; lock resources
Service -> Policy : validate seat semantics
Service -> Price : compute immutable breakdown
note over Price : Quota and reversal decisions remain open.\nSubscription payment uses its separate path.
Service -> State : choose permitted initial state
Service -> PostgreSQL : reserve capacity/visits; persist snapshots
opt CONFIRMED
 Service -> PostgreSQL : award original points once
end
Service -> PostgreSQL : persist outbox and idempotency result; commit
Service --> Route : booking DTO
Route --> User : response
Worker -> PostgreSQL : claim committed outbox record
Worker -> Observer : dispatch event idempotently
Observer -> PostgreSQL : create notification once
Observer -> Mail : send eligible captured email
note over Worker,Mail : Persist retry/send state; never claim universal exactly-once external email delivery.
@enduml
